# Knowledge bundle — how to contribute

This directory is an OKF bundle (`okf_version: "0.1"`). It holds **durable, verified knowledge** about
Policy Atlas — how it's built, how it behaves, and the domain it works in. Conventions, invariants and
pitfalls are where it started; the scope is open (see below).

- **To read it**, start at [index.md](index.md) — the navigational listing.
- **What belongs here:** anything a slice has *proven* that's durable and isn't already another
  lane's job. The test is the bar, not a fixed category list — **types are open**. Not design intent
  (that's `docs/specs/`), not a copy of the specs (link them), not code (link it), not a scratchpad.
- **When to add:** at the after-merge step of the [task cycle](../../.claude/skills/task-cycle/SKILL.md),
  when a merged slice has verified something durable.

## Authoring a concept

One concept per `.md` file. Every concept needs YAML frontmatter:

```yaml
---
type: Convention            # REQUIRED — descriptive, your choice (Convention, Invariant, Runbook, Domain concept, Integration quirk, …); OKF fixes no taxonomy
title: short display name   # recommended
description: one-line summary used in the index   # recommended
tags: [area, topic]         # recommended
timestamp: 2026-06-24       # recommended — date of last meaningful change
---
```

Then a structural body. Favour headings/lists/tables over prose. Cite the source of each claim under
a `# Citations` heading (spec, ADR, code, or test), and link related concepts with markdown links.
Add a line to [log.md](log.md) when you add or materially change a concept.

`index.md` and `log.md` are reserved filenames (no `type` frontmatter). Run `/okf validate` after
editing — every other `.md` in the tree must carry a non-empty `type`.
